# Migrations

Before writing SQL, read the TypeScript that inserts/updates the table. A constraint the writer already violates will 500 production.

- Additive first: create new, keep a shim, merge code, drop old last. Moving/renaming an object without a shim breaks the currently deployed app the moment the migration runs.
- Every new table: RLS policy in the **same** migration.
- Every function/table/sequence: explicit `grant ... to app_runtime`. Advisors only catch "too open", never "app_runtime lost EXECUTE".
- Student-path tables: no hard reject. Unknown codes register `active=false, needs_review=true`.
- **Private schema answer isolation (ADR-017):** correct answers and step payloads live in `private`. `app_runtime` has no direct `SELECT` on `private.*`.
- Grant only objects the live code path actually calls.
- Migration must be applied before the reading code merges to `main`.

## Attempt vs Attempt_Items Schema & FK Invariants
- `public.attempts`: session table (`id`, `student_ref`, `kind`, `started_at`). `kind` (`corpus_soak`, `photo_solve`, `bank_practice`) lives ONLY here; `attempt_items` has no `kind` column.
- `step_events.attempt_id`: references `attempts(id)`, NOT `attempt_items(id)`. Join with `attempt_items` via `ON ai.attempt_id = se.attempt_id`.
- `attempt_items.question_id`: references questions (`question_id`, not `problem_id`).
- `attempt_items.match_path`: supports `'bank'` (Layer 2 Question Bank, 0 cost).
- Dynamic Error Codes: join `LEFT JOIN public.error_codes ec ON ec.code = se.error_code` for official Azerbaijani `title_az`.

